| Piñera participated in [[Hernán Büchi]]'s 1989 presidential campaign and was later elected to the Senate. He was a potential presidential nominee in 1993, but his chances were ruined by a conflict with [[Evelyn Matthei]] that came to be known as ''Piñeragate''. In 1999 he again attempted to be the nominee, but was defeated in the convention by [[Joaquín Lavín]]. In 2005 he shook the political scene by jumping into the first round independently of the UDI. Polls show him narrowly beating Frei in a runoff scenario. He was officially proclaimed by RN on 8 August 2009.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.com/contenido/674_166340_9.shtml |title=Sebastián Piñera es proclamado como candidato presidencial de RN &#124; POLÍTICA |publisher=latercera.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110713190058/http://latercera.com/contenido/674_166340_9.shtml |archive-date=2011-07-13 }}</ref> He submitted his candidacy to the Electoral Service on 9 September 2009.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.com/contenido/654_179733_9.shtml |title=Piñera inscribe candidatura ante el Servel y augura buen resultado de la 'Roja' &#124; PAÍS |publisher=latercera.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=13 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110713190111/http://latercera.com/contenido/654_179733_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref>
|- valign="top"
