| The UDI officially proclaimed Piñera as its candidate on 22 August 2009.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20090822/pags/20090822190033.html |title=Coloma: Piñera es el candidato presidencial de la UDI para dirigir Chile |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> Piñera had been proposed as the party's candidate by the UDI's ''Consejo Directivo'' in December 2008.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20081213/pags/20081213085725.html |title=UDI informó que no pondrán condiciones a Piñera sino "elementos claves" |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref>

Pre-candidates:
*'''[[Evelyn Matthei]]''': She is the daughter of Air Force General [[Fernando Matthei]], a member of the military junta that took power in the [[1973 Chilean coup d'état|1973 coup]]. She was a member of [[National Renewal (Chile)|National Renewal]], but in 1992 was embroiled in a conflict with [[Sebastián Piñera]], ending with her leaving the party and joining the UDI. She has been mentioned as a potential UDI candidate, considering she is among the leading proponents of having the UDI bring its own candidate to the first round. She has said it would be "fun" to compete against Piñera. Longueira said on 9 October 2008 that she would be an excellent candidate. On 11 October 2008, she said she was willing to run for president.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_61341_9.shtml |title=La Tercera - Matthei: "Estoy dispuesta a ser candidata en las próximas elecciones presidenciales" |publisher=Latercera.cl |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090710030641/http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_61341_9.shtml |archive-date=2009-07-10 |url-status=dead }}</ref> She announced her precandidacy on 14 October 2008.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_62451_9.shtml |title=La Tercera - Evelyn Matthei se reconoció precandidata presidencial |publisher=Latercera.cl |date=2008-10-14 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090601070225/http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_62451_9.shtml |archive-date=2009-06-01 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Potential candidates:
*[[File:Lavín crop.jpg|50px|left]]'''[[Joaquín Lavín]]''': He earned a master's degree in [[economics]] from the [[University of Chicago]]. Afterwards, in 1992, Lavín was elected [[mayor]] of [[Las Condes]], a stronghold of the right, with 31% of the vote and reelected in 1997 with 78% of the vote. Lavín was the presidential candidate for the UDI-[[National Renewal (Chile)|RN]] coalition [[Alliance for Chile]] in the [[1999 Chilean presidential election|1999 election]]. He eventually lost to [[Socialist Party of Chile|PS]]/[[Party for Democracy (Chile)|PPD]] candidate [[Ricardo Lagos]] in a runoff by 200,000 votes. Lavín again represented UDI in the [[2005–06 Chilean presidential election|2005 presidential election]], but ended in third place with 23.23% of the vote, due to the presence of another right-wing candidate in the race, [[Sebastián Piñera]], who made it to the runoff election with 25.41% of the vote. [[Pablo Longueira]] urged him to run for a third time for the presidential elections, but he refused and ended up running for a senate seat in the [[Valparaíso Region]] which he lost.<ref>[http://www.emol.com/noticias/nacional/detalle/detallenoticias.asp?idnoticia=280076 Longueira: "Lavín debe ser candidato presidencial" | Emol.com]</ref>
*'''[[Hernán Larraín]]''': He is a senator and former president of the [[Independent Democratic Union|UDI]]. Longueira said on 9 October 2008 that he would be an excellent candidate.

Declined candidacies:
*'''[[Hernán Büchi]]''': A possible candidacy by the 1990 presidential candidate generated buzz within the UDI in June 2007. He has however declined a candidacy.
*'''[[Pablo Longueira]]''': The senator officially launched his candidacy on 30 March 2007. He had announced his plans before the 2005 election took place. He stepped down "momentarily" due to "low party support" on 3 May 2007.<ref>[http://www.emol.com/noticias/nacional/detalle/detallenoticias.asp?idnoticia=254657 Emol.com - Longueira baja por ahora su candidatura presidencial ante escaso apoyo de la UDI]</ref>
*'''[[Jacqueline van Rysselberghe]]''': The mayor of [[Concepción, Chile|Concepción]] was proclaimed, on 11 October 2006, as candidate by five UDI deputies from the Biobío Region. She has refused to campaign for the nomination, however, preferring to concentrate on her 2008 campaign for reelection as mayor. She was reelected as Concepción mayor in October 2008.
