Declined candidacies:
* [[File:Insulza crop.jpg|50px|left]]'''[[José Miguel Insulza]]''': He declared himself a candidate on 12 December 2008.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20081212/pags/20081212094036.html |title=Insulza afirmó que ya lo pueden llamar precandidato presidencial |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |date=2008-12-19 |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> He, however, declined his candidacy on 5 January 2009, and gave his support to Frei.{{Clear}}
* [[File:Lagos crop.jpg|50px|left]]'''[[Ricardo Lagos]]''': His government was highly popular and his term ended with approval ratings around 60-70%. Various supporters urged him to run again in 2009. However, his popularity has lately seen a sharp fall due to the catastrophic new transport system ([[Transantiago]]), planned under his presidency. Lagos has declared all doors are open to him, but has refused to confirm whether he will participate. In March 2008, he said it was unbecoming as a former head of state to participate in a primary and would refuse to do so.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.latercera.cl/medio/articulo/0,0,3255_5664_344614214,00.html | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080327221253/http://www.latercera.cl/medio/articulo/0%2C0%2C3255_5664_344614214%2C00.html|archive-date=27 March 2008 | title=Lagos ratifica que no está disponible para una primaria | language=es | date=24 March 2008 | accessdate=26 August 2024}}</ref> On 8 November 2008, he was proclaimed unanimously by the PPD's National Directive as its candidate, but Lagos never accepted the nomination.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20081108/pags/20081108184756.html |title=PPD proclamó a Ricardo Lagos como su abanderado presidencial |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> On 2 December 2008, the PPD officially proclaimed Lagos as its candidate for the presidency.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.com/contenido/654_80029_9.shtml |title=PPD proclama oficialmente a Ricardo Lagos como candidato presidencial |publisher=latercera.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=13 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110713185327/http://latercera.com/contenido/654_80029_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref> However, two days later, Lagos ruled out running for the presidency, stating in a press conference "I am not, nor will I be, a presidential candidate".<ref name="irishtimes.com">[http://www.irishtimes.com/newspaper/breaking/2008/1204/breaking65.htm Chile's Lagos bows out of presidential race]</ref>
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align:center;"| '''[[Party for Democracy (Chile)|PPD]]'''
| style="text-align:center;"| [[File:Frei crop.jpg|100px|center]]'''[[Eduardo Frei Ruiz-Tagle]]'''
| The PPD selected Frei as its candidate on 24 January 2009, with 296 votes from the party's National Council, against seven for PRSD candidate [[José Antonio Gómez Urrutia]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.emol.com/noticias/nacional/detalle/detallenoticias.asp?idnoticia=341600 |title=Por abrumadora mayoría, Frei es proclamado candidato presidencial del PPD |publisher=Emol.com |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref>{{Clear}}
Other candidates:
* [[File:Bitar crop.jpg|50px|left]]'''[[Sergio Bitar]]''': In a 4 May 2007 interview with ''La Tercera'', he said he was willing to be his party's presidential nominee if there was enough support.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.latercera.cl/medio/articulo/0,0,3255_5664_266873707,00.html |archive-url=https://archive.today/20070802231116/http://www.latercera.cl/medio/articulo/0,0,3255_5664_266873707,00.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=2007-08-02 |title=Bitar dice que está dispuesto a ser carta presidencial del PPD |publisher=La Tercera }}</ref> On 7 November 2008 he said that he is "without a doubt" willing to compete eventually for the presidency, but only if Ricardo Lagos's candidacy does not prosper.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_71247_9.shtml |title=La Tercera - Bitar: "Claro que me la puedo" ante eventual candidatura presidencial |publisher=Latercera.cl |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090211074302/http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_71247_9.shtml |archive-date=2009-02-11 |url-status=dead }}</ref> He declined his candidacy on 10 November 2008, following Lagos's proclamation by his party.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_71675_9.shtml |title=La Tercera - Bitar da paso atrás en su candidatura presidencial en favor de Lagos |publisher=Latercera.cl |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100502055032/http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_71675_9.shtml |archive-date=2010-05-02 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Now that Lagos is out of the race, he may attempt a second run.
* '''[[Nicolás Eyzaguirre]]''': He has said that he could participate if Lagos declines to, but he remained silent after Lagos declined his candidacy.
* [[File:Lagos crop.jpg|50px|left]]'''[[Ricardo Lagos]]''': On 4 December 2008 he ruled out running for the presidency, stating in a press conference "I am not, nor will I be, a presidential candidate".<ref name="irishtimes.com"/>
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align:center;"| '''[[Independent (politics)|Independent<br />candidates]]'''
| style="text-align:center;"| ''None''
| Failed candidacies:
* '''[[Marco Enríquez-Ominami]]''': On 15 December 2008, he announced he was available to compete with Insulza in a Socialist Party primary.<ref name="latercera.com">{{cite web |url=http://latercera.com/contenido/654_84411_9.shtml |title=Enríquez-Ominami se declara disponible para ser candidato presidencial |publisher=latercera.com |date=2008-12-15 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=2011-07-13 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110713185400/http://latercera.com/contenido/654_84411_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref> He, however, did not submit his candidacy to the PS presidential convention. On 9 January 2009, he agreed to compete in the Concertación primaries as independent after gaining the support of some council people and legislators.<ref name="ReferenceA">{{cite web |url=http://latercera.com/contenido/654_91396_9.shtml |title=Enríquez-Ominami acepta ser precandidato presidencial e ir a las primarias de la Concertación |publisher=latercera.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=2011-07-13 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110713185716/http://latercera.com/contenido/654_91396_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref>{{Clear}}
|}

====Primary results====
{{main|2009 Concertación presidential primary}}
The primary was carried out on 5 April 2009 in the [[Maule Region|Maule]] and [[O'Higgins Region|O'Higgins]] regions. Frei became the single Concertación candidate by beating Gómez by a 20-point lead, cancelling the need for further regional primaries.

