===''Juntos Podemos'' candidate===

{| class="wikitable"
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align:center; vertical-align:middle;"| [[File:Juntos Podemos Mas (corto).svg|150px|center]]
| style="text-align:center; vertical-align:middle;"| [[File:Arrate crop.jpg|150px|center]]'''[[Jorge Arrate]]'''<br /><small>([[Communist Party of Chile]])</small>
| The ''[[Juntos Podemos Más]]'' coalition of far-left parties selected former Socialist Party member [[Jorge Arrate]] as its sole candidate for president on 25 April 2009. He was officially proclaimed as candidate on 26 April 2009.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.tercera.com/contenido/674_122454_9.shtml |title=Jorge Arrate es proclamado candidato presidencial del Juntos Podemos &#124; POLÍTICA &#124; latercera.com |publisher=Tercera.com |date=2009-04-26 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=16 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110716211215/http://www.tercera.com/contenido/674_122454_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref> In July 2009, after his candidacy lost the support of the Humanist Party, he became a member of the Communist Party in order to comply with the law and run for president. He submitted his candidacy to the Electoral Service on 9 September 2009.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.com/contenido/654_179777_9.shtml |title=Arrate inscribe candidatura apoyado por dirigenta PS &#124; PAÍS |publisher=latercera.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=13 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110713190126/http://latercera.com/contenido/654_179777_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref>
|}

====Party pre-candidates====
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Party !! Candidate !! Remarks
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align:center;"| [[File:Partido Comunista de Chile.svg|100px|center]]'''[[Communist Party of Chile|PCCh]]'''
| style="text-align:center;"| [[File:Guillermo Teillier headshot.jpg|100px|center]]'''[[Guillermo Teillier]]'''
| Teillier launched his candidacy on 26 September 2008. He said he is willing to step down in order to put forward a single candidate for the ''Juntos Podemos'' coalition of left-parties.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20080926/pags/20080926140157.html |title=PC proclamó a Teillier como su candidato presidencial |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |date=2008-09-26 |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> In November 2008 he said he would be willing to participate in a primary between him, Hirsch and Alejandro Navarro, who had quit the Socialist Party.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_71091_9.shtml |title=La Tercera - Teillier dispuesto a deponer candidatura ante irrupción presidencial de Navarro |publisher=Latercera.cl |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090930184024/http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_71091_9.shtml |archive-date=2009-09-30 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Teillier stepped down as ''Juntos Podemos'' pre-candidate on 25 April 2009, giving his support to Jorge Arrate, saying he was the right person according to the country's political moment.{{citation needed|date=August 2024}}
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align:center;"| [[File:Partido Humanista (corto).svg|100px|center]]'''[[Humanist Party of Chile|PH]]'''
| style="text-align:center;"| [[File:Hirsch crop.jpg|100px|center]]'''[[Tomás Hirsch]]'''
| Hirsch was among the founders of the [[Humanist Party of Chile|Humanist Party]] and vied unsuccessfully for seats in the Chamber of Deputies as part of the ''Concertación''. In 1993, the PH broke off from the coalition. In 1999 he was the Humanist presidential candidate, but lost in the first round. In 2005, he again participated in the presidential campaign, now with the additional support of the [[Communist Party of Chile|communists]]. He garnered a little over 5% of the vote. In an interview with Biobío Radio on 1 September 2007, Hirsch criticized the ''Concertación'' and the Alianza and declared that he would he "happy to be a candidate" if the members of his coalition agree.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.emol.com/noticias/nacional/detalle/detallenoticias.asp?idnoticia=274033 |title=Tomás Hirsch insinúa su entrada al debate presidencial |publisher=El Mercurio Online}}</ref> On 7 June 2008 he announced he intended to run for the presidency for the third time as the PH candidate, under the ''[[Juntos Podemos]]'' umbrella.<ref>[http://www.mer.cl/modulos/catalogo/Paginas/2008/06/08/MERSTNA006CC0806.htm?idnoticia=CE6UJ5GQ120080608 El Mercurio, 8 June 2008].</ref>
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align:center;"| '''[[Independent (politician)|Independent]] (''Socialista-allendista'')'''
| style="text-align:center;"| [[File:Arrate crop.jpg|100px|center]]'''[[Jorge Arrate]]'''
| Arrate is a member of the more leftist faction of the PS and had been mentioned as a potential candidate in an alliance of this faction and the ''[[Juntos Podemos Más]]'' pact. He formally announced his candidacy on 27 January 2008, pressured by a group of socialists opposed to the Socialist Party leadership.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.emol.com/noticias/nacional/detalle/detallenoticias.asp?idnoticia=290290 |title=Ex ministro Jorge Arrate acepta ser precandidato presidencial del PS |publisher=El Mercurio Online}}</ref> On 20 November 2008, Arrate was proclaimed as candidate by a group of Socialist Party Central Committee members.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_76189_9.shtml |title=La Tercera - Proclaman a Jorge Arrate como candidato presidencial |publisher=Latercera.cl |date=2008-11-20 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090731070456/http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_76189_9.shtml |archive-date=2009-07-31 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Arrate resigned from the PS on 14 January 2009.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20090114/pags/20090114155029.html |title=PS recibió sin sorpresa la renuncia de Arrate |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> He was proclaimed as presidential candidate on 18 January 2009 by a group of Socialist Party members, the so-called "socialistas-allendistas".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/un-sector-del-ps-proclamo-a-jorge-arrate-como-candidato-presidencial/prontus_nots/2009-01-18/142119.html |title=Un sector del PS proclamó a Jorge Arrate como candidato presidencial |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref>
|}

====Primary results====
The election to define the sole ''Juntos Podemos'' candidate was carried out on 25 April 2009 in [[Santiago, Chile|Santiago]]. Arrate beat Hirsch and became the single ''Juntos Podemos'' candidate.

