===Independent candidate===

{| class="wikitable"
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align:center; vertical-align:middle;"| [[File:Emblema Marco 2010.svg|150px|center]]
| style="text-align:center; vertical-align:middle;"| [[File:Enríquez-Ominami crop.jpg|150px|center]]'''[[Marco Enríquez-Ominami]]'''<br /><small>(Ind.)</small>
| On 15 December 2008, he announced he was available to compete with Insulza in a Socialist Party primary.<ref name="latercera.com"/> He, however, did not submit his candidacy to the PS presidential convention. On 9 January 2009, he agreed to compete in the Concertación primaries as independent after gaining the support of some council people and legislators.<ref name="ReferenceA"/> He did not submit his candidacy, however. Instead he is running as an independent and as of August 2009, polling above 20% and thus threatening to displace one of the coalition-backed candidates in the expected run-off election. He was proclaimed candidate by the Humanist and Ecologist parties plus several other leftist groups under the banner of a new electoral pact, a New Majority for Chile, on 13 September 2009.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://srv77.hosteur.com/~partidoh/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=481&Itemid=7 |title=Ph Chile - Fuerzas Políticas Proclaman Oficialmente A Enriquez-Ominami |publisher=Srv77.hosteur.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091025120939/http://srv77.hosteur.com/~partidoh/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=481&Itemid=7 |archive-date=25 October 2009 }}</ref> He submitted his candidacy to the Electoral Service on 10 September 2009.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20090910/pags/20090910114641.html |title=Con alusiones a su padre, Enríquez-Ominami oficializó su candidatura |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref>
|}

===Unsuccessful candidacies===

*'''[[Eduardo Artés]]''' ([[Chilean Communist Party (Proletarian Action)|PC (AP)]]): He was proclaimed as a ''Juntos Podemos Más'' pre-candidate by the [[Chilean Communist Party (Proletarian Action)|Communist Party (Proletarian Action)]] on 7 December 2007.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://eduardopresidente.blog.com/?page=2 |title=Eduardo Artés Presidente |publisher=Eduardopresidente.blog.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110708013729/http://eduardopresidente.blog.com/?page=2 |archive-date=2011-07-08 |url-status=dead }}</ref> However, on 26 July 2008, the PC (AP) left the ''Juntos Podemos Más'' pact, accusing them of abandoning their founding principles in light of the pact's electoral deal with the ''Concertación'' for the upcoming October municipal elections.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://eduardopresidente.blog.com/ |title=Eduardo Artés Presidente |publisher=Eduardopresidente.blog.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090907060710/http://eduardopresidente.blog.com/ |archive-date=2009-09-07 |url-status=dead }}</ref> He quit his candidacy in July 2009. He said his candidacy was just an opportunity to present new ideas to the country, as going through with the candidacy would be too economically onerous.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8tb8SQagOrE  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130727105053/http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8tb8SQagOrE |archive-date=2013-07-27 |url-status=dead|title=Eduardo Artés: Lucha Electoral v/s Electoralismo |publisher=YouTube |date=6 July 2009 |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref>
*'''[[Leonardo Farkas]]''' ([[independent (politics)|Ind.]]): A mining businessman.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ireport.com/docs/DOC-147634 |title=Leonardo Farkas; Chile'S Longshot Presidential Candidate Greeted As Hero In Valparasio - Cnn Ireport |publisher=Ireport.com |date=14 November 2008 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090430151516/http://www.ireport.com/docs/DOC-147634 |archive-date=30 April 2009 |url-status=dead }}</ref> On 5 December 2008, he announced he was giving up his presidential candidacy.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.tercera.com/contenido/674_81333_9.shtml |title=latercera.com - Farkas anuncia que no será candidato presidencial |publisher=Tercera.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=16 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110716211111/http://www.tercera.com/contenido/674_81333_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*'''[[Pamela Jiles (journalist)|Pamela Jiles]]''' (Ind.): Journalist and television presenter. She announced her candidacy in February 2009 through a column in ''[[The Clinic (newspaper)|The Clinic]]'' magazine.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://images.lun.com/luncontents/NewsPaperPages/2009/mar/02//LUCPRPO18LU0203_800.swf|title=images.lun.com|access-date=5 May 2009}}{{dead link|date=June 2016|bot=medic}}{{cbignore|bot=medic}}</ref> On 4 September 2009 she stepped out of the race in support of Navarro.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20090904/pags/20090904144543.html |title=Pamela Jiles bajó su candidatura a la Presidencia |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |date=2009-09-04 |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> In the same election, she unsuccessfully ran for a seat in the [[Chamber of Deputies of Chile|lower chamber of Congress]].
*'''[[Luis Molina Vega]]''' (Ind.)<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.independencia2010.cl/ |title=Luis Molina Vega / Una Oportunidad para Los Pueblos de Chile |publisher=Independencia2010.cl |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090304004641/http://independencia2010.cl/ |archive-date=2009-03-04 |url-status=dead }}</ref> A [[civil engineer]] from [[Tomé]]. Molina stepped out of the race in July 2009, due to low support.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.theclinic.cl/2009/07/23/molina-vega-renuncia-a-su-candidatura-presidencial/ |title=The Clinic » Molina Vega renuncia a su candidatura presidencial |publisher=Theclinic.cl |date=2009-07-23 |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref>
*'''[[Alejandro Navarro (politician)|Alejandro Navarro]]''' ([[Movimiento Amplio Social|MAS]]): Navarro used to characterize himself as a leader in the "dissident" faction of the Socialist Party, which harshly criticized what they called the "neoliberal" economic model, supporting instead [[Hugo Chávez]] and [[Fidel Castro]].{{Citation needed|date=October 2009}} Despite his involvement in a scandal due to his participation in a protest organized by the Unitary Workers Central where he attacked a policeman, with the possibility of being expelled from the Senate being considered, Navarro declared himself to be a presidential candidate in 2008. In November 2008, he quit the Socialist Party to form a new party called [[Broad Social Movement]] (MAS). He said his candidacy was necessary to "stop Piñera from winning in the first round", and still considered himself a Socialist.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/prontus_nots/site/artic/20081106/pags/20081106205825.html |title=Navarro: El MAS quiere evitar el bochorno de que gane Piñera |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |date=2008-11-13 |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> The MAS party proclaimed him its candidate on 11 November 2008; the party, however, was still open to stage a primary between all leftist candidates that were not part of the Concertación.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.cl/contenido/23_72559_9.shtml |title=La Tercera - MAS proclama a Navarro como su candidato presidencial |publisher=Latercera.cl |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090524064413/http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_72559_9.shtml |archive-date=2009-05-24 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Navarro has proposed to hold the primary in April 2009.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.latercera.com/contenido/654_77289_9.shtml |title=Navarro llama a candidatos de la izquierda a aceptar primarias abiertas |publisher=La Tercera.com |date=2008-11-23 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=22 May 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110522022342/http://www.latercera.com/contenido/654_77289_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref> On 5 May 2009 Navarro said he would step out of the race and support Arrate if polls released from then to September show the ''Juntos Podemos Más'' candidate having an advantage of seven points over him. He didn't rule out Arrate then supporting Enríquez-Ominami, if his candidacy was the strongest.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://latercera.com/contenido/654_124835_9.shtml |title=Navarro bajará candidatura si Arrate lo supera en siete puntos en encuestas &#124; PAÍS |publisher=latercera.com |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=13 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110713185914/http://latercera.com/contenido/654_124835_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref> Navarro was proclaimed as the official MAS candidate on 25 July 2009 with the support of other minor left groups.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://lanacion.cl/prontus_noticias_v2/site/artic/20090724/pags/20090724210047.html |title=Juez Guzmán y Pamela Jiles apoyan a Navarro |publisher=La Nacion.cl |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090728144018/http://www.lanacion.cl/prontus_noticias_v2/site/artic/20090724/pags/20090724210047.html |archive-date=2009-07-28 |url-status=dead }}</ref> He submitted his candidacy to the Electoral Service on 14 September 2009.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/alejandro-navarro--hemos-llegado-para-quedarnos/prontus_nots/2009-09-14/121840.html |title=Minuto a minuto: La inscripción de Alejandro Navarro |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> On 22 September 2009 Navarro withdrew his candidacy and gave his support to Enríquez-Ominami.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/alejandro-navarro-bajo-su-candidatura-y-entrego-su-apoyo-a-enriquez-ominami/prontus_nots/2009-09-22/145203.html |title=Navarro se bajó y entregó su apoyo a Enríquez-Ominami |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref>
*'''[[Adolfo Zaldívar]]''' ([[Regionalist Party of the Independents|PRI]]): The former president of the Christian Democratic Party and a Senator at the time of his nomination, lost the last internal PDC primary to Alvear. He is the brother of senator and former Interior Minister [[Andrés Zaldívar]]. He was expelled from the PDC in December 2007, later becoming part of the [[Regionalist Party of the Independents]] (PRI). He announced his intention to run as president representing that party, and was proclaimed so on 26 April 2009.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cooperativa.cl/zaldivar-tengo-autoridad-moral-para-decir-que-frei-y-pinera-son-lo-mismo/prontus_nots/2009-04-26/145328.html |title=Zaldívar: Tengo autoridad moral para decir que Frei y Piñera son lo mismo |publisher=Cooperativa.cl |access-date=2010-02-01}}</ref> This decision was ratified on 29 August 2009.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.tercera.com/contenido/654_175226_9.shtml |title=PRI proclama a Adolfo Zaldívar como su candidato presidencial &#124; PAÍS &#124; latercera.com |publisher=Tercera.com |date=2009-08-29 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=16 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110716211303/http://www.tercera.com/contenido/654_175226_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref> He stepped out of the race on 14 September 2009, just hours before the deadline for submission.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.tercera.com/contenido/674_181765_9.shtml |title=Zaldívar baja opción presidencial y declina dar apoyo a otra candidatura &#124; POLÍTICA &#124; latercera.com |publisher=Tercera.com |date=2009-09-14 |access-date=2010-02-01 |archive-date=16 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110716211313/http://www.tercera.com/contenido/674_181765_9.shtml |url-status=dead }}</ref>

==Coalitions for the Congressional elections==
===Concertación and Juntos Podemos Más===
[[File:Chile Aniversario NO-05-10-2009.jpg|thumb|300px|The Former presidents of Chile, together in a Concertación Conference in 2009.]]
The A list conformed after the union of two political coalitions that had taken part separately in the elections of 2005. On one hand the [[Concertación]], which was grouping to the center-left parties that since 1990 governed the country. In the other hand the left-wing [[Juntos Podemos Más]], that it suffered an internal division after the exit of the [[Humanist Party (Chile)|Humanist Party]].

The reason of this strange union was, the [[Binomial System]] that get out the political left from the National Congress since 1994.

The largest party inside the A list was the [[Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|Christian Democrats]], with the leadership of [[Juan Carlos Latorre]] who was chief of the [[Eduardo Frei Ruiz-Tagle|Eduardo Frei]]'s presidential campaign. The [[Socialist Party of Chile|Socialists]] joined with the senator [[Camilo Escalona]], [[Party for Democracy (Chile)|PPD]] with the deputy [[Pepe Auth]]. The [[Social Democratic Radical Party|Radicals]] led by Senator Gómez, and the [[Communist Party of Chile|Communist Party]] with the leadership of [[Guillermo Teillier]].

===Coalition for Change===
[[File:Coalición por el Cambio.jpg|thumb|300px|Presentation of the Coalition for the Change. Fernando Flores speaks.]]

The [[Alliance (Chile)|Alliance for Chile]] for the elections of 2009, began with an important step, by means of I arrive of two precandidates, one of them the senator [[Pablo Longueira]], and the mayor of Concepción, [[Jacqueline van Rysselberghe]], both of the [[Independent Democratic Union]], who demonstrated his availability of postulating to this post, using the regular conduits inside the coalition, nevertheless, both rejected such an option to present only a presidential candidate, who would be [[Sebastián Piñera]].

In March 2009 two Congressmen of the Alliance for Chile obtained the speaker of the Senate and the speaker of the Deputies' Chamber, by means of an agreement with the independent bench and with the [[Concertación|Concert]], respectively. The above mentioned agreements were not lacking in polemic, since the Senator who postulated the alliance to preside at the above mentioned organism, [[Jovino Novoa]], was harshly criticized for personeros of the [[Concertación|Concert]] in view of his past as member of [[Augusto Pinochet]] Ugarte's military regime.

In spite of the critiques, the Alliance for Chile awarded a political victory on having presided at both chambers of the National Congress and some of the most influential commissions of the same one, which, they waited in the conglomerate opponent, he was benefiting Sebastián Piñera's candidacy.

After having integrated the list [[Clean Chile, Vote Happy]], one was generated fail between the charter members of [[ChileFirst]] with regard to the position that would take the party opposite to the presidential and parliamentary elections of 2009. Whereas [[Jorge Schaulsohn]] and Senator Flores supported the candidate of the Alliance for Chile Sebastián Piñera,<ref>Infinita, [http://www.infinita.cl/titulares/despliegue.tpl?fecha=19/03/2009&hora=10:02:37 Schaulsohn se Asume Piñerista] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090524011906/http://www.infinita.cl/titulares/despliegue.tpl?fecha=19%2F03%2F2009&hora=10%3A02%3A37 |date=2009-05-24 }}</ref> the deputy [[Esteban Valenzuela]] rejected to join with the center-right and resigned ChileFirst to endorse [[Marco Enríquez-Ominami]]'s candidacy.<ref>La Nación, [http://www.lanacion.cl/prontus_noticias_v2/site/artic/20090330/pags/20090330131648.html Valenzuela dejó Chile Primero por apoyo a Piñera] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304061942/http://www.lanacion.cl/prontus_noticias_v2/site/artic/20090330/pags/20090330131648.html |date=2016-03-04 }}</ref> The support to Piñera on the part of ChileFirst was made official on 6 May 2009, when one presented the "''Coalition for the Change''", electoral agreement between the Alliance for Chile, ChileFirst and other political minor movements.

===New Majority for Chile===
New Majority for Chile was a political coalition that grouped the [[Ecologist Party (Chile)|Ecologist party of Chile]], the [[Humanist Party of Chile]], and diverse political and independent movements that supported the candidacy of the independent [[Marco Enríquez-Ominami]] for the presidential election of 2009. Between the movements and groups without political legal constitution that they it shaped are the Regionalist Movement,<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20200807182818/http://www.regionalistas.cl/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=30&Itemid=28] Acuerdo entre el el PH, PE, el Movimiento Regionalista, Progresistas en Red y el MUMS</ref> the Movement Unified of Sexual Minorities (MUMS),<ref>http://www.mums.cl/sitio/contenidos/noticias/not_2009_09_14_01.htm {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160305130100/http://www.mums.cl/sitio/contenidos/noticias/not_2009_09_14_01.htm |date=2016-03-05 }} Mums inscribe candidatos por la diversidad sexual al Parlamento</ref> the Movement SurDA and the Progressist Network.<ref>http://www.tomashirsch.cl/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=216:fuerzas-progresistas-alternativas-y-de-izquierda-acuerdan-lista-parlamentaria-que-busca-aglutinar-nueva-mayoria-&catid=9:noticias{{Dead link|date=August 2019 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }} Acuerdan lista parlamentaria para aglutinar nueva mayoría</ref>

